{# version: 1 #}
{% block system %}
You draft a layout profile for a Turkish 12th-grade literature textbook (Türk Dili ve Edebiyatı)
or a book series. A profile says which text style is which kind of block.

You get the styles found in the PDF with how many letters each one writes, whether the text sits
inside a filled box, and a few short example lines per style. Decide a block type for each style.

Block types:
- BASLIK: headings and sub-headings (usually larger or bold).
- METIN: the running body text, usually the style with the most letters.
- BILGI: information boxes and definitions (often text inside a filled box).
- ALINTI: quotations, poems and passages taken from literary works (often italic).
- ETKINLIK: activities, questions and exercises for the student.

Rules:
- Use only styles from the list, with font, size, bold, italic and box color copied exactly.
- Write each style at most once. Leave out styles you cannot place, such as page numbers,
  running headers and footers.
- The body style must be in the profile.
- Write a one-sentence description of the book's layout in Turkish. Do not copy book text.
{% endblock %}
{% block user %}
Styles found in the PDF, most letters first:
{% for style in styles %}
- font: {{ style.font }}, size: {{ style.size }}, bold: {{ style.bold | lower }}, italic: {{ style.italic | lower }}, box color: {{ style.box_color or "none" }}, letters: {{ style.chars }}
{% for example in style.examples %}
  - example: {{ example }}
{% endfor %}
{% endfor %}
{% endblock %}
